Z||000000||penetrator||07-24-2000||10:08 AM||||I read about change the gearfluid to engineoil in a post.<P>I was strictly told to not use anything else than GM manual gear fluid? And i got a problem when i have been driving a really long ride. When it gets hot it starts to sound<BR>                                really strange, like the gears are threading over(but the car still draging(accelerating)). <BR>                                So can i really change the oil to engine oil?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||07-24-2000||12:45 PM||||The owner's manual calls for 5W30 engine oil to be in the 4spd Muncie in my 85SE V-6.  I believe that is the case for all of the Fiero manual gearboxes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-24-2000||12:48 PM||||p.s.<P>I'd be wary of advice from whoever told you to use gear oil in your trans.  These cars are different from most cars in some respect and general info doesn't always apply.<P>Have a great day,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||07-24-2000||01:31 PM||||Here's what GM recommends:<P><B>Automatics:</B> Use Dexron ATF (imagine that?!)<P><B>4-speed Muncie:</B> 5W-30 engine oil (per 1986 owner's manual).<P><B>5-speed Getrag:</B> GM initially recommended 5W-30 engine oil; sometime in 1988 they changed the recommendation to  GM Synchromesh Fluid, P/N 12345349.  I would recommend it for the 4-speeds, too.  <P>In a pinch, engine oil, ATF or even salad oil is probably better than nothing.  But I use the Synchromesh Fluid.  At $8/qt, it's expensive, but I use it because it's what GM recommends, and it's really pretty cheap insurance.  The Synchromesh Fluid was developed for the purpose - compatible with composite synchros, seals, and so forth.<P>I bought my GT from a guy who had taken it to a transmission shop for a clutch job.  By the time they got through, they sold him a brand new Getrag from the factory, and managed to disable the speedometer and cruise control.  They also filled the transaxle with ATF, and plugged the fill tube with a ground off dipstick from an automatic.<P>No idea how much they charged for all this "service," but needless to say, the previous owner was happy to sell me this "money pit."  I got the car home, drained the ATF, replaced it with Synchromesh Fluid, bought the proper dipstick from a dealership, and re-crimped spade terminals they had used for the speedometer sender (what do you bet these "experts" forgot to disconnect the connector when they dropped the cradle?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ).  Now, the speedometer and cruise control worked.  <P>In fairness, there are no doubt plenty of good transmission shops around   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  And I can understand the confusion about which lube to use, because the OEM's changed their recommendations several times over the years   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !<P>So there's my long-winded advice.  GM Synchromesh Fluid in everything but automatics.  Unless your tranny seals leak   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||penetrator||07-24-2000||02:55 PM||||Thanks for all the answers.<P>I think i have the GM Synchromesh Fluid in now. It was expensive and was 1 qt in each bottle (Dont have the bottle here so i cant check the numbers). And the bottle was white with, i think, blue GM logo on. But the car still sounds crazy when the tranny is hot, and it sounds like when you dont use the clutch when i shift gears, and it sounds also when i have the 1st-3rd gear in postition. And am i going to break the transmision if i continue to drive (It dosent sound like that when im driving in the city or shorter distances) I think mine is a Izusu 4-speed(86) cos it looks like that one in the Chilton repair manual.<BR>So if i am going to change to engine oil, what kind of oil should i use: syntetic, mineral oil or what?<P>Thanks Again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phantom Rage||07-24-2000||04:07 PM||||I too, was wondering what about which fluid to use.  Great info Stugood, but how about an 88 Isuzu?  <P>Here is the info I ran across, hope this helps.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ida.net/users/cm2/lubebsk7.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ida.net/users/cm2/lubebsk7.htm</A> ||||reg||7
